# NORDIC HAMSTRING CURL

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Nordic Hamstring Curl is a bodyweight eccentric knee-flexion exercise designed to maximize hamstring strength, eccentric force production and posterior chain resilience.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the highest-value exercises for injury prevention and eccentric strength development.

---

# Philosophy

Combat athletes repeatedly accelerate, decelerate, kick, sprint and change direction.

These actions expose the hamstrings to extremely high eccentric loads.

The Nordic Hamstring Curl specifically prepares the hamstrings to tolerate these demands.

CAS selects this exercise when robustness and long-term athlete availability are priorities.

